			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Closing the HTML window from the parent macro ([Rect] sub_QuickSnap)
Yes — the parent macro can close it.

After you display the preview (asynchronously) and after your Keep/Retake prompt, add:

Set Variable rect_closePreview to Text
1
The HTML polls rect_closePreview every ~200ms; as soon as it sees 1, it closes itself.

Optional: auto-close after N seconds
Instead of closing from the parent macro, you can set:

rect_autoCloseSeconds = 2 (or 3, etc.)
</string>
